     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for adults in a hospital is 3,200 mg/day, and that is the ceiling, not a typical dose.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It would be a serious overdose even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for pain or inflammation.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common upper-range dose.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, please confirm that and give the clinical reason. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
